WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Lean in close to a curved make-up mirror.

2
00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.760
Your face looks back upright,
and larger than life.

3
00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:10.540
Now step back a few paces and
look at the wall behind you.

4
00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.000
In the same mirror, that wall
hangs upside down, and smaller.

5
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:16.000
Same mirror.

6
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:17.810
Just a few steps apart.

7
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.410
Two completely different images.

8
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.070
So what decides whether an
image is upright or upside down,

9
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.810
bigger or smaller?

10
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.640
In this mission, you'll draw
three special rays from an object,

11
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.420
and find exactly where its image forms.

12
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:36.090
Then you'll use the mirror equation
to calculate where an image is,

13
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.020
and how tall it is.

14
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:43.080
Your mission: find out what decides which
kind of image a curved mirror makes.
